    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3056907": {
      "title": "Greenville University",
      "description": "Greenville University - Adjunct Faculty – Digital Media (On-Campus Preferred | Exceptional Remote Candidates Considered) In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Adjunct Faculty – Digital Media (On-Campus Preferred | Exceptional Remote Candidates Considered) Greenville University Apply Adjunct Faculty – Digital Media (On-Campus Preferred | Exceptional Remote Candidates Considered) Greenville, IL • Faculty Apply Description Greenville University is seeking passionate, creative, and student-focused adjunct instructors to teach courses within our growing Digital Media program. We are primarily seeking instructors who can teach on campus in a face-to-face environment , creating engaging, hands-on learning experiences for students. However, we also recognize exceptional talent comes from many locations and will consider outstanding remote candidates with a proven record of excellence in teaching and industry practice. Courses May Include: Web Page Design Digital Photography Digital Video Production Animation Digital Art Other Digital Media courses based on expertise and program needs About the Opportunity As an Adjunct Instructor, you will help prepare the next generation of creative professionals by combining industry knowledge, practical skills, and meaningful mentorship. We welcome applications from educators, designers, content creators, photographers, videographers, animators, and digital media professionals who are excited to share their expertise in a Christ-centered learning environment. This position reports to the Digital Media Program Coordinator. Requirements Master's degree in Digital Media, Design, Communications, Visual Arts, or a related field; or an equivalent combination of education and professional experience Demonstrated expertise in one or more Digital Media disciplines Strong teaching, presentation, and communication skills Ability to organize and deliver engaging, student-centered instruction Experience using learning management systems such as Canvas, Blackboard, D2L, or similar platforms Commitment to continuous improvement and instructional best practices Excellent interpersonal and collaboration skills Understanding of and commitment to Greenville University's mission and the value of Christian higher education Preferred Qualifications Previous college-level teaching experience Professional experience in creative, digital, or media-related industries Experience teaching in both in-person and online environments Location & Teaching Format Our strongest need is for instructors who can teach on campus in Greenville, Illinois , where students benefit from hands-on collaboration, studio-based learning, and direct faculty engagement. That said, we know great educators can make an impact from anywhere. Exceptional candidates who are only available to teach remotely are encouraged to apply. Remote opportunities will be considered based on course needs, candidate qualifications, teaching effectiveness, and professional experience. Why Teach at Greenville University? Invest in the lives and careers of emerging creative professionals Join a collaborative, mission-driven academic community Bring real-world industry experience into the classroom Help students develop both technical excellence and professional character Contribute to a Christ-centered educational environment that values creativity, service, and purpose Application Process Please submit the following materials: Curriculum Vitae (CV) or résumé outlining educational background, teaching experience, and professional accomplishments Statement of Philosophy of Christian Higher Education Statement describing your personal faith journey and commitment Official or unofficial higher education transcripts Applications will be reviewed as materials are received and will remain open until the position is filled. Compensation The regular undergraduate adjunct rate for courses with enrollments of 10 or more students is $1,000 per credit hour ($3,000 per 3 credit class on avg) . Compensation may vary based on course enrollment and program needs. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY employer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment Visa at this time. Greenville University's Mission: Greenville University is liberal arts University that empowers students for lives of character and service through a transforming Christ-centered education. Our hiring practices reflect our commitment to be a Christ-centered institution. GREENVILLE UNIVERSITY : The university is located 50 miles east of St. Louis in an attractive residential community of approximately 7,000 people. Greenville was founded in 1892 and is affiliated with the Free Methodist Church yet draws students from 40+ denominations. For additional information, please visit our website: www.greenville.edu . Greenville University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, sex, disability, family responsibilities, or  national or ethnic origin, in employment opportunities, in keeping with applicable state and federal laws. In keeping with the mission of the institution, Greenville University seeks applicants with a strong commitment to the values and lifestyle of evangelical Christianity and who profess a personal relationship with Jesus Christ. As a Christian institution, we require faculty and staff to adhere to the University's Lifestyle statement and to enforce a religiously based code of conduct for all University employees. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Greenville University, as an educational institution affiliated with the Free Methodist Church USA, reserves the right to prefer employees on the basis of religion (Title VII, Sections 702-703, United States Civil Rights Act of 1964 as amended). Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software"
